==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|apprize||archaic}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/əˈpɹeɪz/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-appraise.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪz|s=2}}
* {{hyph|en|ap|praise}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|apreisen}}, from {{der|en|fro|aprisier||apraise, set a price on}} (compare modern {{cog|fr|apprécier}}), from {{der|en|la-lat|appretio|appretiare}}, from {{m|la|ad-}} + {{der|en|la|pretium||price, value}} (English {{m|la|precious}}), from which also {{doublet|notext=1|en|appreciate}}, a doublet.

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[determine]] the [[value#Noun|value]] or [[worth#Noun|worth]] of (something), particularly as a [[person#Noun|person]] [[appoint]]ed for this [[purpose#Noun|purpose]].
#: {{synonyms|en|q1=archaic|apprise|q2=archaic|apprize|evaluate|Thesaurus:appraise}}
#: {{co|en|to '''appraise''' goods and chattels}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[consider]] comprehensively.
#: {{synonyms|en|interpret|look upon|think of|Thesaurus:deem}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[judge]] the performance of someone, especially a worker.
#: {{ux|en|At the end of the contract, you will be '''appraised''' by your line manager.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[estimate]]; to [[conjecture]].
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[praise]]; to [[commend]]. <!--obsolete?-->
#: {{synonyms|en|exalt|laud|venerate|Thesaurus:glorify}}

